Derived from PSllama d079717, GPL-3.0-or-later.

PS5 Vulkan and output-buffer tuning switches for the NexusAI llama.cpp pin
620d2225, stacked on 0101-0103. Every switch is opt-in: with none set, behaviour
is identical to upstream.

  GGML_VK_RM_KQ=<n>      rows per workgroup for k-quant mat-vec shaders (default: upstream heuristic)
  GGML_VK_RM_IQ=<n>      rows per workgroup for i-quant mat-vec shaders (default: 2 * RM_KQ)
  GGML_VK_DMMV_WG=large  force the 4-subgroup dequant mat-vec workgroup (default: heuristic)
  PS5_OUTPUT_CPU_BUFFER  keep the output logits in CPU memory, not the device host buffer

Context refreshed to 620d2225: rm_iq in ggml_vk_load_shaders (ggml-vulkan.cpp ~2890),
the two DMMV workgroup heuristics (~5602, ~5690) and llama_context::output_reserve
(src/llama-context.cpp ~2308).

